# agent-kit app.config — EXAMPLE
#
# Copy this to `<your-app>/.claude/app.config` and fill in your app's paths.
# It is a plain KEY=value data file (one key per line). It is READ, never
# `source`d — a committed config a gate consumes must not be able to run
# arbitrary shell.
#
# FORMAT RULES:
#  - Comments (`#`) must be on their OWN line. An inline `KEY=val # note` is NOT
#    supported — the `# note` becomes part of the value.
#  - The value is everything after the first `=`, with leading/trailing
#    whitespace trimmed (internal spaces are preserved, e.g. a space-separated
#    list). On a duplicate key the FIRST occurrence wins.
#
# CONTRACT: every key is OPTIONAL. A check/gate whose key is UNSET is SKIPPED,
# never failed — so the shared `preflight.sh` + `merge-gate.mjs` run unchanged
# across every app; each app supplies only the keys that apply to it. With no
# app.config at all, preflight runs only its generic checks (exit 0) and
# merge-gate runs only its app-agnostic gates (C4/staging-merge/P2/C5).
#
# The values below are ZIEE's — a Rust(+cargo workspace)/React(npm workspaces)
# monorepo. A different app (e.g. a Python/TS app) sets a different subset.

# ── preflight.sh (Phase-1 environment gate) ───────────────────────────────
# A build-embedded seed file that makes the build PANIC if absent.
PREFLIGHT_SEED_FILE=src-app/server/binaries/hub-seed/index.json
# One-line fix hint printed when the seed is missing.
PREFLIGHT_SEED_HINT=rm -rf src-app/server/binaries/hub-seed && cargo check -p ziee (refetch), or cp it from another clone
# A vendored git submodule that must be initialized before the build.
PREFLIGHT_SUBMODULE=src-app/server/vendor/pgvector
# npm workspaces (space-separated) that hoist to the repo-root node_modules.
PREFLIGHT_NODE_WORKSPACES=src-app/ui src-app/desktop/ui
# Env var name that toggles per-worktree build-DB isolation (=0 disables it).
PREFLIGHT_BUILD_DB_ENV=ZIEE_BUILD_DB_PERWORKTREE
# host:port of the local build-DB cluster (used to detect an external override).
PREFLIGHT_BUILD_DB_HOSTPORT=127.0.0.1:54321
# (optional) an extra committed DATABASE_URL sentinel treated as "local".
PREFLIGHT_BUILD_DB_SENTINEL=sqlx-build-sentinel
# Dev-config auto-seed: dir, the real (gitignored) file, its committed example,
# and the placeholder secret value the app hard-refuses to boot on.
PREFLIGHT_CONFIG_DIR=src-app/server/config
PREFLIGHT_CONFIG_FILE=dev.yaml
PREFLIGHT_CONFIG_EXAMPLE=dev.example.yaml
PREFLIGHT_CONFIG_PLACEHOLDER=dev-secret-change-in-production-min-32-chars-long

# ── merge-gate.mjs (merge-time gate) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Migrations dir → C2 migration-collision + --verify-head duplicate-prefix.
MERGE_MIGRATIONS_DIR=src-app/server/migrations
# Cargo package for the C1 clean-build gate (`cargo clean -p <pkg> && cargo check`).
MERGE_CARGO_PACKAGE=ziee
# (optional) dir to run cargo from; default probes src-app/ then src-app/server/.
MERGE_CARGO_DIR=src-app
# (optional) a second cargo package checked only when the desktop prefix is touched.
MERGE_CARGO_DESKTOP_PACKAGE=ziee-desktop
MERGE_DESKTOP_TOUCH_PREFIX=src-app/desktop/tauri/
# Codegen regen command → C3 regen-parity + C6 generated-coverage.
# C3 runs MERGE_REGEN_CMD in the merged staging tree and then asks GIT what
# changed — over the WHOLE tree, NOT scoped to MERGE_GENERATED. That is
# deliberate: scoping the parity diff to a hand-maintained list has exactly the
# failure mode the gate exists to prevent (cytoanalyst's regen writes five files
# against a two-entry list, so three generated files could be merged
# side-taken/stale and still pass). With an unscoped diff the guarantee — a
# generated file is a function of its inputs, so REGENERATE, never take a side —
# holds for every output, declared or not.
MERGE_REGEN_CMD=just openapi-regen
# The EXPECTED generated set. Now documentation + the C6 audit target, not the
# scope of C3: C6 derives what the regen actually WROTE (stat-stamp diff across
# the run) and FAILS when it writes a path this list does not name — so the next
# added output is loud, not silent. C6 SKIPs (explicitly, never PASSes) when the
# regen rewrites nothing, i.e. when the set cannot be derived.
# ALSO consumed by lifecycle-check.mjs: every declared path joins its
# generated-file exemption (diff classification + FE-touch detection) on top of
# the built-in openapi.json / api-client/types.ts patterns, so a regen-only
# diff stays classified backend even when the regen writes more than those two
# files. Unset ⇒ the built-in patterns only (historical behavior).
MERGE_GENERATED=src-app/ui/openapi/openapi.json src-app/ui/src/api-client/types.ts src-app/desktop/ui/openapi/openapi.json src-app/desktop/ui/src/api-client/types.ts
# (optional) paths/dirs the regen may dirty WITHOUT failing C3 parity — e.g. a
# lockfile a build legitimately refreshes. Space-separated, repo-relative; a dir
# entry covers everything under it. Empty by default: anything the regen touches
# is treated as generated output the gate is responsible for.
#MERGE_REGEN_IGNORE=Cargo.lock
# STAGING PROVISIONING. `git worktree add` materializes the TRACKED tree ONLY, so
# the staging tree the heavy gates build from is missing two things the real
# working tree has — and C1/C3 then fail SPURIOUSLY (a provisioning gap, NOT a
# check failure):
#  1. submodule working trees are EMPTY (a crate sourced from a submodule ⇒
#     `failed to read <submodule>/…/Cargo.toml`). merge-gate therefore runs
#     `git submodule update --init --recursive` in staging whenever the merged
#     tree has a .gitmodules. Set to 0 to opt out (default: 1, no key needed).
#MERGE_STAGING_SUBMODULES=1
#  2. GITIGNORED per-machine files (e.g. a dev config the codegen needs ⇒ regen
#     dies with `no config file found`) are absent by definition. Declare them
#     here — space-separated repo-relative paths, files or dirs — and merge-gate
#     copies each from the LIVE repo into staging. Nothing app-specific is baked
#     into the shared gate; an absent declared path is WARNED about and the run
#     continues, so the gate needing it still fails for its real reason. Only
#     UNTRACKED paths are copied — a TRACKED path is refused (the merged tree
#     already holds the authoritative version; overwriting it could mask a
#     genuine C1/C3 failure).
MERGE_STAGING_COPY_FILES=src-app/server/config/dev.yaml

# Repo-relative DIRECTORIES mirrored from the source repo into staging as a tree
# of symlinks (never copied — these are gigabytes; never hard-linked either, so a
# build writing into node_modules/.cache cannot corrupt the source repo).
# Workspace SELF-links are re-pointed at staging: a single symlink to the whole
# node_modules would make `@app/ui -> ../../src-app/ui` resolve into the SOURCE
# tree, and the check would grade the wrong code, mostly green. This exists for `node_modules`: a staging
# worktree is the TRACKED tree only, so any gate that shells out to npm/tsc dies
# with "command not found" or "Cannot find module" — a FALSE RED indistinguishable
# from a real regression. Same TRACKED-path refusal as COPY_FILES.
# Unset = no directories linked (and C7 will fail for a node-based check).
MERGE_STAGING_LINK_DIRS=node_modules src-app/ui/node_modules

# ── C7: the app's OWN check recipe, run on the MERGED tree ────────────────
# C1 is `cargo check`; C3 is regen parity. NEITHER runs the repo's own `check`
# target, so every gate wired into it — stale-brand lints, doc-reference checks,
# design-token drift, testid-registry parity, frontend `tsc` — is invisible to
# the merge gate. Measured: a DOCS-ONLY branch passed all nine gates and turned
# `just check` red on main, because prose is exactly what a prose-grading lint
# grades and nothing at merge time ran one.
# Runs after C3/C1, only on a completed merge; skipped by --skip-heavy.
# Unset SKIPS the gate.
MERGE_CHECK_CMD=just check

# ── lifecycle-check.mjs (per-phase gate) ──────────────────────────────────
# lifecycle-check is otherwise app-agnostic; only these three ziee-specific
# values are read from app.config. EACH KEY DEFAULTS TO ZIEE'S HISTORICAL
# HARD-CODED VALUE (shown below) — so ziee behaves identically whether it sets
# the key or omits it, and a differently-laid-out app overrides just what differs.
#
# Frontend npm workspaces, as ordered `<path-prefix>:<workspace-label>` pairs
# (space-separated). A changed/planned file whose path starts with a prefix
# belongs to that workspace; FIRST match wins, so list the more-specific prefix
# first. Drives the phase-3 e2e-tier requirement + the phase-8 per-workspace
# `npm run check (<label>): PASS` gate. An app with ONE frontend sets one pair;
# a pure-backend app can set an empty/absent value (the FE gates then never fire).
LIFECYCLE_FRONTEND_WORKSPACES=src-app/desktop/ui/:desktop/ui src-app/ui/:ui
# openapi.json spec paths (space-separated) forming the live /api route registry
# that the R2-5 e2e route-mock-staleness gate validates static `page.route('**/api/…')`
# mocks against. Absent/unbuilt specs ⇒ R2-5 SKIPs (nothing to check against).
LIFECYCLE_OPENAPI_SPECS=src-app/ui/openapi/openapi.json src-app/desktop/ui/openapi/openapi.json
# Working-tree path substrings the A2 clean-tree gate ignores (noisy vendored
# submodules etc.), space-separated. `*.log` scratch files are always ignored
# on top of this. Default = ziee's vendored pgvector submodule.
LIFECYCLE_CLEAN_TREE_IGNORE=vendor/pgvector

# LIGHT-tier size threshold: the maximum number of changed lines (added+deleted
# in base...HEAD, excluding .lifecycle artifacts and generated openapi/types) a
# diff may have and still qualify for the LIGHT track. Size is necessary but not
# sufficient — any ONE of {new permission, migration, new module, public
# API/schema change} forces HEAVY regardless of size. LIGHT requires the core
# artifacts and ONE audit round; every deterministic hardening check runs in
# both tiers. Default 800 — a review-capacity judgement (two angles saturate
# somewhere in the high hundreds of lines), not a blast-radius one.
LIFECYCLE_LIGHT_MAX_LINES=800
